  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, has died following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. Lomas was paralysed from the chest down after being thrown from her horse at the Osberton Horse Trials in 2007, breaking her neck, back and ribs and puncturing a lung. She went on to raise nearly £1m for charity through various events, most notably completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit. She was subsequently chosen to light the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square that year. In 2016, she completed the Great North Run while pregnant, also wearing her bionic suit. Her family have asked for privacy as they grieve."
